   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: LGD formed a committee to prepare the standard operating procedure for institutionalizing criteria-based fund transfer.

UGIAP approved and being implemented in 88 (cumulative) pourashavas

38 pourashavas approved gender- and climate-responsive O&amp;M management system

1,564 pourashava staff (including 90% of eligible women staff) reported increased knowledge on the selected topics including UGIAP, GESIAP, etc.

GESIAP adopted and being implemented with 1.0% budget earmarked from own revenue by 88 pourashavas.

1,517 residents from low-income neighborhood enrolled in skills development training, of which 380 already completed training and the remaining are in progress

128 LINIC has been formed in 23 pourashavas with more than 80% women members

Consultant recruitment for four packages have been completed and the preparation of the 61 climate and disaster risk-informed master plans are in progress.

LGED&apos;s web-based revenue management system is now functional. Data migration for 21 PSs completed and another 17 PSs is ongoing.

The guideline has been approved by LGED and disseminated in 88 pourashavas.

257 detailed designs have been completed in 63 pourashavas.

81 contracts have been awarded for 122.20 km of drainage rehabilitation and reconstruction

34 contracts have been awarded for 415.16 km of roads rehabilitation and reconstruction

Contracts have been awarded for seven (7) climate-resilient, and GESI-inclusive public facilities remodeling or developing

Preparation of the sub-packages have been completed for 23 pourashavas with more than 50% women participation</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
